<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The community is operated as a senior housing
operating property (&ldquo;SHOP&rdquo;). Following the acquisition, revenues are expected to be generated primarily from resident fees
and services, including amounts earned under resident agreements for monthly rental charges, care and healthcare-related services, and
other ancillary resident care. Resident fees and services are expected to be billed monthly based on contracted rates set forth in the
resident agreements and recognized as the related performance obligations are satisfied. The community includes resident homes and related
common areas, site improvements, furniture, fixtures and equipment, and resident lease in-place intangible assets.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The Company utilizes an independent third-party
operator to manage the day-to-day operations of the community pursuant to a management agreement. The operator is responsible for staffing,
resident care, marketing, billing and collections support, maintenance, compliance with applicable laws and regulations, and preparation
of property-level operating information. The Company retains oversight and approval rights over significant operating and capital matters.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>Note 2 &ndash; Summary of Significant Accounting
Policies</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><I>Basis of presentation</I></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The accompanying Statement of Assets Acquired
and Liabilities Assumed (the &ldquo;Statement&rdquo;) presents the assets acquired and liabilities assumed of The Riviera Alexandria as
of June 1, 2026. The Statement has been prepared in accordance with accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America
(&ldquo;GAAP&rdquo;) for the purpose of complying with Rule 3-05 of Regulation S-X promulgated by the Securities and Exchange Commission
(&ldquo;SEC&rdquo;). Pursuant to the SEC staff&rsquo;s waiver relief under Rule 3-13 of Regulation S-X, the Statement is being provided
in lieu of the historical financial statements otherwise required under Rule 3-05 of Regulation S-X.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The Statement is not intended to present the Company&rsquo;s
complete financial position, results of operations, changes in equity, or cash flows in accordance with GAAP on a standalone basis. No
historical revenues or expenses are presented because the Statement is limited to the assets acquired and liabilities assumed as of the
acquisition date and, prior to the community&rsquo;s opening in March 2026, there were no material operations to report.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></P>

